  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sexual and reproductive health and rights solutions via Healthy Entrepreneurs in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite the progress made in recent years in improving health outcomes, access to good quality health care remains a major challenge for Ethiopia, especially at community level. Issues explaining this situation include understaffed facilities, un(der)paid and undercapacitated health workforce and improper functioning of supply chains for health products and services.This project seeks to contribute to a solution to this situation by enabling the organization Healthy Entrepreneurs to introduce its Community Health Entrepreneurs model in Ethiopia and to capacitate a first group of Community Health Entrepreneurs who as self-employed entrepreneurs provide health products and services to beneficiaries in their communities. In this way, Healthy Entrepreneurs will be enabled to establish herself in Ethiopia and to build the conditions to upscale its operations to a scale that will help the model to become financially self-sustainable in the longer-term.</narrative>
  </description>
